I disagree; I frequently die on Astral, because I've been playing
underprepared recently because I find it more fun. If you have an AC of
0 or so + half phys and spell damage, a unihorn, and maybe 3 or 4
sources of full healing (counting both potions and life saving), and
no weapon but an Excalibur at +3 or so, you can typically get around 1
and a half altars through Astral, but not far enough to complete it.

(However, I believe that if you add conflict, a fully enchanted
Excalibur, and a +3 katana as an offhand weapon, you can get past all
three altars with the same resources. I actually did something like
that recently.)


Of course, if you overprepare, Astral is trivial, but then so is
everywhere else. An overpreparing ascension is over at the Castle, if
not earlier.

